    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Skull-Faced Servant",
      "category": "defensive",
      "text": "A servitor phantom's head is that of an animal skull, as determined by their original role in the castle before the curse fell. This skull head grants the servitor phantom a horns or jaws Strike (as appropriate). Each type of skull is associated with a different Lore skill.\n\nBrewers have deer skulls and Alcohol Lore.\n\nCooks have bird skulls and Cooking Lore.\n\nHousekeepers have cat skulls and Labor Lore.\n\nValets have dog skulls and Labor Lore."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Susceptible to Death",
      "category": "defensive",
      "text": "Though phantoms aren't alive, neither are they undead, and they are uniquely vulnerable to the effects of death.\n\nA phantom whose Hit Points are reduced to 0 as a result of a death effect (such as from a spell like Execute) is immediately whisked away to the River of Souls, where their soul resumes the usual path to the afterlife."
    },
